foundation.solution_text:
The cylinder unrolls into two circles and a rectangle:
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.5]
\draw (0,0) rectangle (6.3,4);
\node at (3.15,2) {curved surface};
\node[below] at (3.15,0) {$2\pi r$};
\node[right] at (6.3,2) {$h$};
\draw (8.4,3.1) circle (1);
\node at (8.4,3.1) {$\pi r^{2}$};
\draw (8.4,0.9) circle (1);
\node at (8.4,0.9) {$\pi r^{2}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
$A = 2\pi r^{2} + 2\pi rh$
$= 2\pi(4)^{2} + 2\pi(4)(9)$
$= 32\pi + 72\pi$
$= 104\pi$
$= 326.7256\ldots$
$\approx 326.7\text{ cm}^{2}$

